From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: AC-3 and E-AC-3 passthrough

Adds the decisions of the compressed passthrough sink. On tvOS only
AVPlayer renders the Atmos objects carried in E-AC-3, so spdif-ac3 and
spdif-eac3 go to an AVPlayer that reads the bitstream through a resource
loader (bound in patch 0016); every other spdif format is still refused,
so mpv decodes it.

- ao_avfoundation_iec61937.h and .c turn mpv's IEC 61937 stream back into
  the plain bitstream: burst scanning (data type, payload length,
  completeness), byte swapping, the syncword check, and the stream window
  the loader serves from, keeping 2 MiB of history below the oldest
  reader. Bursts that fail a check are logged and skipped.
- ao_avfoundation_compressed.h and .c run the sink: a feed step on every
  timer tick, loader request, start and unpause; filling to
  compressed-lead ahead of the later of the item's timebase and
  currentTime (twice that before playback moves), behind the prefetch
  guard and the window's backpressure; the item's clock and the end times
  mpv takes as its audio clock, built from the carrier frames consumed;
  diagnostics; serving decisions; and the fallback that blocks the format
  for the process and asks mpv to reopen audio as PCM. After a fallback
  every feed step does nothing.

A start after mpv's end of file resumes feeding the same item and logs
"resuming compressed feed after audio EOF". The sink's logs keep the
formats and levels Vivid reads.

